                <pb facs="0582" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Baker, Charles/42: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-26T11:00:00+08:00">March 26, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 26—3:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Hankow’s 45, March 24, 2 p.m. I question the propriety of our suggesting that
                    flood relief wheat be used to obtain Baker’s release. If the Chinese Government wishes to use it for
                    that purpose it can do so on its own initiative.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
